{
  "name": "Steady Aim",
  "type": "feat",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Your aim becomes deadly. As a Bonus Action on your turn, you can take careful aim at a creature you can see that is within range of a ranged weapon you're wielding. Until the end of this turn, your ranged attacks with that weapon gain two benefits against the target:</p><ul><li>The attacks ignore half and three-quarters cover.</li><li>On each hit, the weapon deals additional damage to the target equal to 2 + half your fighter level.</li></ul><p>You can use this feature three times. You regain all expended uses of it when you finish a Short or a Long Rest. Additionally, you can spend one use of your Second Wind to regain one use.</p>",
